PRIORITY FIX: Contextual Topic Persistence + Co-Reference Resolution
Problem

Meeting summaries currently lose conversational context across longer discussions and transcript chunks.

Examples:

“the server” should resolve to “SCCM server” if SCCM is the active topic.
“the button” should resolve to “Waypoint Utility Account Creation button.”
Multiple aliases for the same object are not normalized.

This causes:

vague summaries
weak action ownership
loss of operational meaning
poor continuity across chunk boundaries
Goal

Implement semantic topic persistence and contextual inference across the entire meeting pipeline.

The system should maintain active conversational entities and resolve ambiguous references based on:

current topic
recent topic history
semantic similarity
participant context
system/application references
Desired Behaviors
Co-Reference Resolution

Examples:

“the server” → “SCCM server”
“that tool” → “Waypoint Utility Account Creation Tool”
“the button” → “bulk utility account request button”
Topic Continuity

The model should understand:

topic continuation
topic expansion
topic switches
returning to previous topics
Alias Normalization

Normalize references such as:

bulk request button
utility account create button
utility tool
bulk utility tool

Into:

“Waypoint Utility Account Creation Tool”
Proposed Architecture
Pipeline
Transcription
Transcript cleanup
Entity extraction
Topic tracking
Co-reference resolution
Semantic normalization
Final summarization
Action item inference
Confidence scoring
